From fee90fc237796237a578150abb482a5e952e84bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:27:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban create overlap: compare a creator's own open
 cards; dedup same-run re-issues; count same-creator duplicates

Problem: on 13 Nov (hub default board), three times a dispatcher card created a second card for work its
own earlier card already covered, and each duplicate ran a worker until it noticed:

| First card | Duplicate | Creator | Gap | First key | Duplicate key |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| t_01a1d44c7b488318 09:45:44Z | t_01a1d44d9e68cca4 09:46:59Z | t_01a1d43457d48e65 | 75 s | none | followup:pr2058:review-nits |
| t_01a1d4914914925a 11:00:53Z | t_01a1d4917584d038 11:01:05Z | t_01a1d46d21ec8bd3 | 12 s | none | followup:pr2110:review-nits |
| t_01a1d462ff5c8698 10:10:20Z | t_01a1d4e145f389a5 12:28:15Z | t_01a1d41fd158579d | 2 h 18 m | none | pr2062-nit-session-kanban-continue-own-result |

The last duplicate ran 12:28-13:05Z, opened PR #2237 and closed it as superseded by 5b7202e08e.

Why 1: no guard stopped the second create. `_find` skipped every open card "the same chat or the same
worker created (fan-out)" (hermes_cli/kanban_overlap.py module docstring and the `creator_task_id == self_tid`
skip in `_find`). The idempotency key could not match either: each first create had no key.
Why 2 (checked against each creator's worker_result last_output and card comments; the transcripts are on
worker-6/7, unreachable from here):
- 12 s and 75 s pairs: the creator followed the placement remedy for a card kept local by a marker
  ("kanban_archive the unclaimed card ... and re-create it"). The archive was refused because a worker had
  already claimed the first card, and the creator re-created anyway, adding a key. Evidence: the 12 s
  creator's comment ("my archive+recreate to drop a placement marker failed because both were claimed
  instantly"); the 75 s creator's last output ("A worker had already claimed that follow-up card before I
  tried to recreate it, so I created duplicate card t_01a1d44d9e68cca4"). A core_update_pause restart in
  the 75 s run came after both creates (1794563501 vs 144/219), so it is not the cause.
- 2 h pair: the creator, in a later run, filed a review nit on `_answer_interrupted_calls` /
  `with_own_result` while its round-1 child t_01a1d462ff5c8698 (same fix site) was open and claimed; the new
  body names neither that child nor any check of open children.
Why 3 (instructions): the worker protocol's remedy (agent/prompt_builder.py "Created cards") said to archive
and re-create, with no condition that the archive succeeded.
Root (happened): the fan-out exemption treated every card from the same creator as deliberate fan-out, so
the overlap guard never saw a creator's own duplicate, whatever its title or gap.
Root (not caught):
- Each duplicate was caught only by the duplicate's own worker, after it had already built the same change.
  t_01a1d4e145f389a5 ran for 37 min and opened PR #2237 before it noticed.
- Nothing at create time compared a new card with its creator's open cards, because of the fan-out
  exemption.
- Nothing afterwards counted cards closed as a duplicate of a sibling from the same creator, so 3 in one day
  went unnoticed until an owner chat looked.
- (hypothesis, checked: confirmed) The overlap tests had no same-creator duplicate case.
  `test_same_chat_fan_out_and_parents_are_not_matches` covers only `parents`, and the singleton "self" case
  is the creator's own card, not a card it created.
Recurrence: a repeat, 3 times on 13 Nov (table above). No earlier fix targeted this exemption;
t_01a1d4dc5eb85b00 fixed the opposite case (a false refusal against an origin mirror). The 10 Nov pair
t_01a1c78af452ff15 / t_01a1c78addfc72e4 was two different creators racing, another cause.

Countermeasures:
- root: a card the same creator task made is no longer exempt (hermes_cli/kanban_overlap_own.py). It meets
  the normal match (titles, files, failures) and the existing admits (waits on, recovers, cites, distinct
  target), then four same-creator admits: another assignee; review vs non-review title; different leading
  component tags ([core]/[mods], Board:/Core:); enumerated titles (index markers that differ: w1-01/w1-02,
  worker-2/3, 1/3 vs 3/3, fixture A/B). A new match form, same creator only, catches a duplicate worded
  apart: at least 3 shared snake_case identifiers, each named by at most 2 other open cards, and title word
  ratio at least 0.3. `distinct_from` still overrides. The same-chat (session) exemption stays for cards
  another creator made. proof: tests/tools/test_kanban_create_overlap_same_creator.py replays the 3 pairs and
  14 real legitimate same-creator fan-outs from the same 7 days (fixture from the hub sync-shadow board,
  including the background cards that name the same identifiers). All 3 are refused and all 14 admitted; on
  the old code the 3 duplicate cases fail (match is None) and the fan-outs pass.
  Replay of all 1654 same-creator pairs of the 7 days (first card open when the second was created) through
  the real `_find`: 11 refused (2 of them deduplicated). They are the 3 above, 7 real or partial duplicates
  (one exact-head review of PR1160 at bcbc371e20 filed twice; the 894ddbe34 ancestor readback filed twice;
  the PR1111 natural-polling verification filed twice, 3 h apart; failed-result observer restarts twice;
  two review-nit rounds on #1792; hub claim-screen follow-ups that #1810/#1811 split; the state-suite pair)
  and 1 false refusal (two "Fixture: ... pickup independent verification" cards, which `distinct_from`
  passes). Removing the exemption outright would refuse 517.
- symptom (Do 4): a same-run re-issue returns the first card. When the match is a title match, the first
  card was created by the same creator during its current run (task_runs.started_at), has no idempotency
  key, and the title ratio is at least 0.8, kanban_create returns {ok: true, created: false, deduplicated:
  true, task_id: <first>} and records a `create_overlap` event with outcome `deduplicated`; the CLI prints the
  first id with exit 0. The 12 s and 75 s pairs dedup; the 2 h pair (another run) is refused with the usual
  note. proof: test_same_run_reissues_deduplicate_and_the_later_round_is_refused and
  test_worker_reissue_in_the_same_run_returns_the_first_card (through the real kanban_create tool).
- instructions: the worker protocol now says to re-create only once the archive succeeds; a refused archive
  means a worker claimed the card, so keep it.
- detection: hermes_cli/kanban_dup_detector.py, called after each completion commits. When a completion's
  summary or result says it duplicates or was superseded by a card id, and that card has the same creator,
  one open card collects the pattern: created when none is open, a comment on it otherwise, a new card once
  it is done or archived. The guard alone does not make this redundant: it is a heuristic (shared title
  words or 3 rare identifiers), and a duplicate worded apart with no shared identifier still passes it.
  proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dup_detector.py replays the 3 recorded completion summaries and opens
  exactly one card (two comments); another creator's duplicate and a plain completion open nothing.
