+    "body": "Follow-up from exact-head review 5888975887 on PR #2058 (https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2058#pullrequestreview-5888975887), example-org/hermes, base `state`, file `hermes-sync`. PR #2058 merged as eb032c4aed.\n\nNon-blocking nits to address:\n1. A missing install-stamp.json raises FileNotFoundError, which fetch_peer_partial treats as transient, so it recopies on every pass. Decide: a complete copy with no stamp is a verify-class failure (memoize), or skip the peer cheaply before copying.\n2. Stamp JSON that is not a dict raises AttributeError and escapes (pre-existing). Treat it as a verify failure.\n3. The codesign calls in verify_prebuilt_app have no timeout. Add them so the 2 h .peer-partial-tmp keep window bounds verify.\n4. A transient `codesign -dv` failure reads as ad-hoc and is memoized (pre-existing). Distinguish a nonzero exit or timeout (transient, do not memoize) from a real ad-hoc signature.\n\nAdd a test for each. Open one PR against `state`, get an independent exact-head review, and merge on green CI.",
