+    "body": "Follow-up from exact-head review 5889811976 of PR #2110 (https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/2110#pullrequestreview-5889811976), card t_01a1d46d21ec8bd3. Repo example-org/hermes, base branch `state`, file hermes-sync.\n\n1. Waiter path can still wait on a copy: if Desktop quits while the detached peer-partial copier (spawned under `taskpolicy -b`) is in flight, the waiter's apply blocks under apply.lock in `fetch_peer_partial(wait=True)` until the copy finishes (bounded only by PEER_COPY_TIMEOUT_S + verify, ~1 h). Fix: run the copier at normal QoS, and/or have the waiter apply with wait=False when a local ready/last_ready build already serves something, deferring otherwise. Test: Desktop-quit apply with a live in-flight copier marker does not block on it.\n2. Pin race: a detached copier finishing between `served_partial_target()` (which runs verify_prebuilt_app/codesign) and `pin_build()` can clear last_ready and `_prune_after_peer_partial` the chosen build. Fix: pin rec[\"sha\"] inside served_partial_target before the verify. Add a test.\nOptional: `_fetch_peer_partial_locked` state.json read-modify-write without build.lock (cosmetic).\n\nKeep #2043/#2058/#2110 semantics (build.lock/apply.lock, peer-partial.lock, PEER_PARTIAL_FAILED memo, .peer-partial-tmp prune exemption). Acceptance: RED-on-base unit tests in tests/test_core_bootstrap_up_to.py or sibling, 3 acceptance modules (test_core_bootstrap_up_to, test_core_partial_apply, test_core_reclaim_lease_extension) pass with HERMES_TEST_CORE set and skipped=0, mutant killed, exact-head independent review, merge on green CI.",
