+    "body": "Read-only victim scan for t_01a1cf477dece56b (acceptance f). Run it on **this machine** (worker-2) and report the counts.\n\nBackground: kanban park probes (`wake_check`) used to go through the display secret redactor before they were stored. A probe containing `idempotency_key='\u2026'`, `*_token=\u2026` or a similar name could be stored masked (`\u2026`, `***`, `\u00abredacted`), and then it never matches. The fix is in PR #1354. This scan finds live probes that are already damaged.\n\nRun this exactly, read-only (`mode=ro`). Never edit `task_wake_checks` rows.\n```\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport glob, os, re, sqlite3, socket\npat = re.compile(r\"(?i)[a-z0-9_]*(?:key|token|secret|password|passwd|credential|auth)[a-z0-9_]*\\s*[=:]\\s*['\\\"]?[^\\s'\\\"]*?(?:\\.\\.\\.|\\*\\*\\*|\u00abredacted)\")\ndbs = glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.hermes/kanban.db\")) + glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.hermes/kanban/boards/*/kanban.db\")) + glob.glob(os.path.expanduser(\"~/.hermes/profiles/*/kanban.db\"))\nlive = victims = 0\nfor db in dbs:\n    try:\n        rows = sqlite3.connect(f\"file:{db}?mode=ro\", uri=True).execute(\"select task_id, cmd from task_wake_checks\").fetchall()\n    except sqlite3.Error as e:\n        print(db, \"ERR\", e); continue\n    live += len(rows)\n    for tid, cmd in rows:\n        if cmd and pat.search(cmd):\n            victims += 1; print(\"VICTIM\", db, tid, pat.search(cmd).group(0)[:60])\nprint(socket.gethostname(), \"dbs\", len(dbs), \"live_wake_checks\", live, \"victims\", victims)\nEOF\n```\nFor each VICTIM line, comment on t_01a1cf477dece56b (or ask an operator to) with the task id and the masked fragment, and do NOT print the full command. A victim's owner must re-park with a correct probe; do not rewrite the row.\n\nComplete with metadata `{\"host\": \"<hostname>\", \"dbs\": N, \"live_wake_checks\": N, \"victims\": N, \"victim_task_ids\": [...]}`, and put the printed final line in the summary.",
