+    "id": "t_01a1ceb4f46658c8",
+    "title": "Backfill pre-fix attachment bytes from worker-3 to Board blob store (52 hub rows)",
+    "body": "## Goal\nCopy the bytes of hub attachment rows that were completed on **hermes-worker-3** before its core had the worker-attachment-custody fix (daveey/hermes c2b5952cca, PR1161) up to the Board blob store, under their ORIGINAL uid, so the hub can read them through the normal attachment path. Follow-up from t_01a1ca91167d8889 (backfill acceptance item 3).\n\n## Why these rows don't self-heal\nWorker kanban mirrors drop finished cards. A row whose card finished before the fix was installed never got a blob_key, and its local row is now gone, so `transfer_pending` can't upload it. The files usually still exist under `~/.hermes/kanban/attachments/<task>/[<uid>/]<filename>`. On worker-2 this recovered 12 of 12 rows (all hub-verified).\n\n## Snapshot (hub, 2026-11-12 ~07:40Z)\n52 rows on this host (claim lock `hermes-worker-3:*`): hub `/home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/t_01a1ca91167d8889/gaps-hermes-worker-3.json`, sha256 `0b8bce024bda039e331de156c9e97941d8e9b61dd34c2b45d193b1fc94c332c1`.\n\n## Steps\n1. Confirm that this host's installed core contains the fix: `git -C ~/.hermes/hermes-agent merge-base --is-ancestor c2b5952cca73cbc5b9f4ce4030566089796a09ca HEAD`. If it doesn't, `kanban_schedule` with that command as `wake_check` (awaiting kind=deploy, hermes-core-update). Uploads need the installed `Hub.put_attachment`. Hub evidence says worker-3 started uploading blobs at ~07:21Z, so it's probably installed already.\n2. After install, take a fresh gap list, since rows can be added until install: `hub-admin \"sqlite3 -json ~/.hermes/kanban.db \\\"select a.uid,a.task_id,a.filename,a.size,a.created_at,(select coalesce(json_extract(e.payload,'\\$.lock'),'') from task_events e where e.task_id=a.task_id and e.kind='claimed' and e.created_at<=a.created_at+5 order by e.id desc limit 1) as claim from task_attachments a where coalesce(a.stored_path,'')='' and coalesce(a.blob_key,'')=''\\\"\" > hub-gaps.json`. Keep only `claim` starting with `hermes-worker-3:` (jq). If `hub-admin` is missing here, use the snapshot file above, fetched through any hub read you have.\n3. `scp -O hub-admin:/home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/t_01a1ca91167d8889/worker_gap_backfill.py .` and check its sha256 is `83fd9e5d66c22bc9d6399523f12b6edcb167f6c7545db61a9ba2e52b452ebf0e`. Run `python3 worker_gap_backfill.py hub-gaps.json results.json --dry-run`, then run it again without `--dry-run`. The script only matches by task/filename/exact size, uploads under the hub uid, then GETs the blob and compares bytes. It never writes a DB. A `hub 429` means rate-limited: wait about 60 s and rerun only the failed rows.\n4. Hub-side check: `scp -O results.json hub-admin:/home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/t_01a1ca91167d8889/results-hermes-worker-3.json`, then `hub-admin \"cd ~/.hermes/hermes-agent && HERMES_HOME=/home/ubuntu/.hermes .venv/bin/python /home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/t_01a1ca91167d8889/hub_verify_uids.py /home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/t_01a1ca91167d8889/results-hermes-worker-3.json\"`. Every uploaded row must print `normal_read_verified`.\n5. Complete. Report the count of uploaded+hub-verified rows and name every `no_local_source` or `size_mismatch` row (uid, task, filename) as unavailable on this host. Attach results.json and the verify output.\n\nOut of scope: the 31 historical worker-1 rows (old host 192.0.2.17 is offline). Don't touch the DB directly, and don't create new attachment rows.",
