+    "title": "[core] Unloaded sweeper + producer admission: per-process residual for live chats, host pass under host_loop_lease (design t_01a1d45d75851804 \u00a72b)",
+    "body": "Design: comment 62984 on t_01a1d45d75851804 \u00a71 (unloaded/producer rows) and \u00a72b, review items R1\u2013R4. Depends on t_01a1d470ec8f86ca (`hermes_cli/host_loop_lease.py`). Evidence: `kanban_unloaded._loop` = 14.9% of a steady hub serve's samples, 10.1% of the gateway's; `producer_admission._loop` 3.9% of a serve; started in every web-server process (`hermes_cli/web_server_app.py:120-138`) plus the gateway.\n\nWhat to build:\n- Split `kanban_unloaded._loop` into (a) a **residual pass every process runs** restricted to its own `live_session_ids()`: `delegation_unloaded` and `notice_guarantee` deliveries for chats live here (today they return `skipped:held` from any other process, so these must stay per-process); and (b) a **host pass** gated by lease `kanban-unloaded` (`lease.held()` at top of pass, `lease.beat()` per pass): `sweep_remote_once`, `sweep_once`, the not-held parts of delegation/guarantee, `notice_fanout.card_change_pass`, `reap_notices.retry_pending_killed_notices` iterated over `_stores()` (today it only gets `server._get_db()`).\n- `notice_fanout`: move `_cursors` and `_remote_snapshot` to a host-durable table (state.db or kanban home) so a lease hand-off does not drop one interval (today the first pass is baseline-only).\n- Holder wake capacity: `MAX_PARALLEL_WAKES` for unloaded/guarantee/delegation becomes 8 in the holder (config knob); running out of slots rewinds the claim and retries next pass instead of writing a passive row (`skipped:slots`). Document that the per-chat wake budget (`HERMES_KANBAN_UNLOADED_WAKES_PER_HOUR`) is now host-wide.\n- `producer_admission._loop` `sweep_once` gated by lease `producer-admission`; `deliver_pending` from the per-chat poller unchanged.\n- Roles: gateway registers priority `gateway`, Desktop serve `serve`, always-on dashboard `dashboard`.\n- Kill switch `HERMES_HOST_LOOP_LEASE=0` restores today's behaviour.\n\nDone when: RED\u2192GREEN tests: a chat live in a non-holder process still gets its delegation/guarantee delivery from its own residual pass; an unloaded chat is delivered exactly once by the holder; hand-off keeps notice_fanout outcomes (no dropped interval); slot exhaustion retries rather than writing a passive row; killed-notice retry covers every store. Existing kanban_unloaded/producer_admission/notice_guarantee/delegation_unloaded suites green. Land via `hermes-core-wt ship` with an independent exact-head review card (verdict + reviewed_sha + reviewed_pr).",
