+    "title": "[mods] chat-closeout: per-process residual for live chats, host ledger scan under host_loop_lease (design t_01a1d45d75851804 \u00a72b)",
+    "body": "Design: comment 62984 on t_01a1d45d75851804 \u00a71 (chat-closeout row) and \u00a72b, review item R1. Depends on t_01a1d470ec8f86ca (core `hermes_cli/host_loop_lease.py`) being on main. Evidence: chat-closeout `_loop` (`wake_tick`, `owner_wake_tick`, `watchdog_tick`, `reconcile_done`/`_cols`) = 9.4% of a steady hub serve's samples, 4.4% of the gateway's; every process scans the same host ledger each 30 s, but `server._wake_session_turn` only succeeds where the chat is live (`refused` elsewhere).\n\nWhat to build (hermes-mods `plugins/chat-closeout`):\n- Residual pass in every process: wakes/relays only for ledger rows whose chat is in this process's `live_session_ids()` (cheap indexed read, not a full scan).\n- Host pass (full pending scan, reconcile_done, owner_wake for chats no process holds, watchdog candidate scan) only when lease `chat-closeout` is held; `lease.beat()` per pass. Probe the core API with `getattr`/ImportError: an older core keeps today's behaviour (safe duplication). The watchdog's existing `Ledger.lease(\"watchdog\")` posting gate stays.\n- Hooks (`pre/post_llm_call`, `pre_final_gate`) and the sidebar waiting source are per-turn and unchanged.\n\nDone when: RED\u2192GREEN tests in `plugins/chat-closeout/tests`: a chat live in a non-holder still gets its close-out wake from its residual pass; a cold chat is woken once by the holder; old core (no lease module) = today's behaviour. Land on hermes-mods main per the hermes-mods-repo skill (PR, required CI green on exact head, independent exact-head review card with verdict + reviewed_sha), then confirm it is live on the hub (hermes-mods-repo-testing).",
