+    "body": "Independent exact-head review of https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1260 at head 5d2e512cbb5dea43b7be3fd8887a3a11520a497b (implementer card t_01a1ce7ed2addb09; you must not be that card's session).\n\nBackground: a Kanban \"blocked; needs attention\" wake is rendered when the card blocks, then can wait in a chat's admission FIFO for hours. The PR re-reads the card at delivery (`gateway/session_ingress.execute_admission` -> `hermes_cli/kanban_stale_ask.refresh_payload`, producer rows only). When the card has moved past the block, the \"Next action for the user\" and \"Why only the user\" lines become one `Since then: ... No action needed.` line. A card still blocked on the same block keeps the text byte-identical, and any doubt leaves the text unchanged.\n\nRound 2 (t_01a1cee06436bbba, head cba1de5f14) approved with three non-blocking findings. The branch has since been rebased onto origin/main, and the new commit 5d2e512cbb addresses them:\n- N1: a scope that quotes an `Open task: @task:<b>/<other>` line redirected the read to <other>. Fix: each field stops at the next field's line mark, and a second `\\nOpen task: ` before the notice ends (blank line / next actor line) makes the notice ambiguous, so it is left unchanged. Tests: test_open_task_line_inside_scope_does_not_redirect_the_read (RED on cba1de5f14), test_open_task_line_inside_scope_of_a_done_card_is_left_alone.\n- N2: quadratic backtracking (3000 lines took about 3.9 s). Fix: fields cannot contain the next mark, which makes the match linear. Test: test_pathological_producer_text_is_bounded (<0.5 s; RED on cba1de5f14 at 3.9 s).\n- N3: legacy tui_gateway `_kanban_pending` is not covered. Disposition: the observed 22:14 PST notice was MacBook state.db session_admissions seq 3264, request_id [\"kanban-wake\",\u2026], local_automation_v1 set, so it went through execute_admission. The legacy path is a separate follow-up card, not this PR.\n\nTask: trace `git diff d1af1dff3c~1..5d2e512cbb` (focus on commit 5d2e512cbb in hermes_cli/kanban_stale_ask.py and its tests) and report what you observe. Check that N1 and N2 are resolved and that no regression appears in the earlier behaviour: still-blocked notices stay byte-identical, the stray-mark and joined-notice cases hold, and the user-terminal hint is still swallowed. Run `hermes-core-wt test tests/gateway/test_kanban_stale_block_ask.py tests/tui_gateway/test_actionable_block_notices.py` from a detached worktree of that sha. Then do one adversarial pass that tries to refute your own findings, and report only the findings that survive it.\n\nComplete with kanban_complete metadata: `verdict` (approve | request_changes), `reviewed_sha` = 5d2e512cbb5dea43b7be3fd8887a3a11520a497b, `reviewed_pr` = https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1260, `findings` list. If you cannot comment on t_01a1ce7ed2addb09, put the findings in metadata. Remove any worktree you add.",
