+    "body": "Follow-up from t_01a1ce7ed2addb09 (PR https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1260, review finding N3).\n\nPR1260 re-reads a queued block notice's card at delivery, but only on the gateway admission path: `gateway/session_ingress.execute_admission` -> `hermes_cli.kanban_stale_ask.refresh_payload`. The legacy tui_gateway path renders texts at collection time (`tui_gateway/session_notifications.py` `_notif_collect_kanban`, `_kanban_pending`, `_notif_poll_kanban_scoped` -> `_kb_persist_batch` -> `_notif_submit(\"\\n\".join(fresh))`), so a notice buffered there behind a busy turn can still show a stale \"Next action for the user\" ask.\n\nContext: the incident on 11-11, t_01a1cd4dbbc27e50 notice at 22:14 PST, went through the admission path (state.db session_admissions seq 3264), not this one. First check whether this path still delivers in practice: grep MacBook desktop/agent logs for `__notif__` submits in the last 7 days. If it is dead, say so with evidence and close the card.\n\nIf it is live: apply `hermes_cli.kanban_stale_ask.refresh_stale_ask` to the batch text before it is persisted to the transcript and submitted. Keep the per-text `_KanbanText` attributes (_kb_keys, _kb_blocked, _kb_remote). Remote `@task:<b>@<gw>/` notices stay unchanged, which is already the module's behaviour.\n\nAcceptance: write predictions first. A RED test shows a blocked text buffered in `_kanban_pending` while the card finishes still carrying \"Next action for the user\"; it must FAIL first. GREEN with the fix. A still-blocked control stays byte-identical. Land via `hermes-core-wt ship` with exact-head review, then request review.\n\nDepends on PR1260 having landed (needs hermes_cli/kanban_stale_ask.py on main).",
