+    "body": "Part 1 of 3 of the approved plan on t_01a1d0d37a4d1780 (David chose \"Go: build as planned\"): Throughput panel Tokens breakdown by model.\n\nRepo: daveey/hermes-hub (local ref checkout ~/code/_ref/hermes-hub; work in your own worktree/clone).\n\n## Wire format (decided, shared with the core card \u2014 do not change)\nMachine metrics payload gains an OPTIONAL field:\n`tokens_by_model`: object `{ \"<model>\": [io_total, cache_total] }`\n- cumulative monotone totals, same semantics/units as the existing scalars `tokens_io_total` / `tokens_cache_total` (the per-model sums equal those scalars)\n- <= 32 keys; key: non-empty string <= 64 chars; values: exactly 2 integers in [0, 1e15]\n- senders fold overflow models into the key `other` and map empty model to `unknown` (Board just validates)\n\n## What to build\n- worker/src/mailbox.ts: extend validation (METRIC_BOUNDS today rejects unknown fields) to accept `tokens_by_model` with the bounds above; reject (400) malformed values: >32 keys, long/empty name, non-int, negative, >1e15, wrong arity. Absent field keeps current behaviour.\n- Pass it through unchanged in the registry metrics the Board returns for each machine (wherever `tokens_io_total` is surfaced today, e.g. /v2/machines).\n- Tests in worker/test/machines.test.ts: accept valid, each rejection case, round-trip through the registry read, old payload unaffected.\n\n## Done when\n- worker tests pass (name the count); PR merged with required CI green; Board deployed using the repo's normal deploy path, and a live readback shows a POSTed `tokens_by_model` coming back in the registry (use a test machine/your own gateway's metrics, not a fake production entry that lingers).\n- Complete with summary + PR URL in metadata.published_pr. The plugin card (part 3) is parented on this one.",
