+    "body": "Part 2 of 3 of the approved plan on t_01a1d0d37a4d1780 (David chose \"Go: build as planned\"): Throughput panel Tokens breakdown by model.\n\nFile: hermes_cli/machine_throughput_metrics.py (Hermes core fork). Ship via the normal `hermes-core-wt ship` flow (review + CI) per the loaded skills.\n\n## Wire format (decided, shared with the Board card \u2014 do not change)\nAdd OPTIONAL field to the machine metrics payload:\n`tokens_by_model`: `{ \"<model>\": [io_total, cache_total] }`\n- computed from `session_model_usage GROUP BY model` summed over every state.db the sender already reads for `tokens_io_total` / `tokens_cache_total`; use the SAME columns as those scalars so per-model sums equal them exactly\n- empty/NULL model -> `unknown`; model name truncated to 64 chars (merge collisions)\n- <= 32 keys: keep the top 31 by io_total+cache_total, fold the rest into `other`\n- ints, clamped to [0, 1e15]\n\n## Compatibility\n`send_compatible` must drop `tokens_by_model` and retry once when an old Board answers 400 (Board support lands in a sibling card; this card does NOT wait for it \u2014 build and ship now).\n\n## Done when\n- Unit tests: grouping, unknown mapping, truncation/collision merge, 32-key fold to `other`, sum equals scalars, 400 -> retry without field. Name test file + count.\n- Shipped through hermes-core-wt ship with review + CI green; complete with summary and PR/commit in metadata (published_pr if a PR). The plugin card (part 3) is parented on this one.",
