+    "title": "core: Kanban restart-continuation should keep a stopped call's own result below the interrupted stamp (sibling of PR #2062)",
+    "body": "Follow-up from review 5889241381 on example-org/hermes PR #2062 (t_01a1d41fd158579d).\n\nPR #2062 made `agent/update_pause_cancel.committed` keep a cancelled tool call's own result below the update stamp (`with_own_result`: head 1536 + tail 512 chars, closing `[end of the cancelled call's own result]` line). The sibling path `gateway/session_kanban_continue._answer_interrupted_calls` (restart continuation of a Kanban run) still overwrites each stopped tool row (`_stop_result_rows`) with the bare `interrupted_result(at)` text, so a killed command's own `[Command interrupted]` partial output (e.g. a Terraform apply log, a job_id) is still dropped there.\n\nFix: in `_answer_interrupted_calls`, for each stopped row being rewritten, read its current content and, when it is the tool's own text result (not the executor's cancel/skip text), write `with_own_result(stamp, own)` instead of the bare stamp (reuse the helper from agent/update_pause_cancel.py). Appended rows for unanswered calls keep the bare stamp. Add a test in tests/ next to test_kanban_restart_continuation. Land via `hermes-core-wt ship`.",
