+    "title": "core follow-up: update_pause_cancel.with_own_result should treat executor's emit_cancelled JSON as no own result (PR #2062 review nit)",
+    "body": "Review t_01a1d49b9d56482f of PR #2062 (review 5890290599) raised a non-blocking nit.\n\nIn the hermes-agent fork, `agent/update_pause_cancel.with_own_result` keeps a cancelled call's own result below the update-pause stamp. It already skips the executor's bracketed `[Tool execution cancelled/skipped \u2014` texts. But `ToolCall.emit_cancelled` (agent/tool_executor.py ~:290) builds `{\"error\": \"Tool execution cancelled. ...\", \"status\": \"cancelled\"}` JSON, and that JSON would be kept below the stamp as if it were the call's own result. That is noisy, and the docstring says it should not happen.\n\nFix: treat a JSON result whose `status == \"cancelled\"` and whose error starts with \"Tool execution cancelled\" as having no own result, so the bare stamp is returned. Add a test in tests/tui_gateway/test_update_pause_mid_tool.py. Land via `hermes-core-wt ship` (core-wt new <slug>, exact-head review, `--review-task`).",
