+    "title": "Terraform 1a W3: Energy filter 3/3, read the results and write energy-balance.md (plan Task 16b, Fable)",
+    "body": "Terraform milestone 1a, Wave 3 (gods without a model, plan Phase 3), Task 16b part 3 of 3: read the energy filter's results. Orchestration spec: `docs/HANDOFF.md` in example-org/coworld-terraform (hub checkout `~/code/coworld-terraform`). The text below is copied from the plan at commit 95253d6 (Task 16b; Step 3 is yours, with the second half of Step 4).\n\nInputs: `experiments/energy/results/balance-allowance.csv`, `balance-life.csv`, `balance-sacrifice.csv` and their README on main (run card `t_01a1cb1bce567be5`; if it could not push, they are attachments on it: commit them first, unchanged). Also read design 4.9, `tools/balance.nim`, and the plan review's probe (`docs/reviews/gate1-plan-review.md`, B1 and S1).\n\n## What to write\n\nDesign 4.9: before any model plays, check with scripted gods whether an energy source can be broken. This is a\nfilter. The default is chosen in Phase 8 with a model playing; until then it is the allowance.\n\nFor each `EnergySource`, each `Objective` and seeds 1000-1019 it plays: heuristic, do-nothing, bad, spammer,\nthe all-out culler, the careful culler, hoarder, and the late-starting heuristic (`newRun(seed, objective, source)`), and prints one CSV row per\nsource and objective with the mean score of each god, the heuristic's energy spent by action kind, and the\ncorrelation between energy spent and score across gods. Then, per source, the five checks of design 4.9:\n\n1. no exploit god (spammer, either culler, hoarder) has a higher mean score than the heuristic\n2. heuristic > do-nothing > bad\n3. the late-starting heuristic scores at least 70% of the heuristic\n4. no one action kind takes more than 80% of the heuristic's spend\n5. the god that spends most is not the god that scores most, or two gods within 10% of each other's spend differ\n   by more than 20% in score\n\nThe careful culler is the exploit design 4.9 prices against: \"maximize rabbits by killing every fox\", stopped\njust short of the extinction that scores zero. The all-out culler alone would hide it. In the plan review's probe\n(seeds 1000-1009, Allowance, `maximize_rabbits`) the all-out culler lost on mean score (2120 against the\nheuristic's 3040, do-nothing 2365) only because 4 of its 10 runs ended in extinction. On the 6 seeds where a fox\nsurvived it beat the heuristic on every one (mean 3533 against 3022). So expect the Allowance to fail check 1\nagainst the careful culler at the current prices. That is a finding for `energy-balance.md` and for the choice\nof source and prices in Phase 8. It is not a reason to change the check, the floor or the culler.\n\n**Step 3: Write `docs/spikes/energy-balance.md`** (Fable reads the CSV)\n\nThe table, which sources pass all five, and for a failing source which god broke it and how. A source that fails\nis not removed: it is reported, and Phase 8 runs only the sources that pass. If no source passes check 1, say\nso plainly with the numbers and stop there: block the Fable card with a `human_request` (the options are a higher\nkill price, a score that counts foxes, or accepting the exploit for 1a). Do not change a price in this task.\n\n**Step 4: Commit**\n\n```bash\ngit add tools/balance.nim docs/spikes/energy-balance.md\ngit commit -m \"Scripted energy filter: three sources against exploit gods\"\n```\n\n## Done when\n- `docs/spikes/energy-balance.md` is committed and pushed to main: the table (source x objective x god, mean scores), the 15 check results with their numbers, which sources pass all five, and for each failing source the god that broke it and how. Every number in it is in the CSVs; say which file and row.\n- `metadata` has `sources_passing` (list) and `check1_failures` (source -> god).\n- If no source passes check 1: the write-up is still committed and pushed first, then this card is blocked with `kanban_block(kind=\"needs_input\", human_request=...)` whose `action` names the three options from the plan (a higher kill price, a score that counts foxes, accepting the exploit for 1a) and says what unblock and archive mean, and whose `evidence` quotes the `CHECK` lines. Phase 8 is the consumer of this decision; Wave 4 does not wait on it.\n- Branch and worktree removed.\n\n## Rules (from docs/HANDOFF.md; read it and the plan before starting)\n- Spec: `docs/plans/2026-11-10-terraform-1a-plan.md` (the task named above, verbatim; if main's text of that task is newer than the copy in this body, main wins) and `docs/plans/2026-11-10-terraform-design.md` (rev 4). Repo `example-org/coworld-terraform` (private), main branch. Engine `example-org/polyworld` pinned at `6fe65dc38ec24579907d10c8c427957e6ee6218f` (its `terraform` branch). If the files are missing on your host, `git clone git@github.com:example-org/coworld-terraform.git`; never implement from memory.\n- The \"Decided. Do not reopen.\" list in HANDOFF.md is fixed. If you find one of those decisions is wrong, stop and report on this card (kanban_block with the evidence); do not route around it.\n- Test first: write the test, run it, see it fail, then write the code. Commit after each task.\n- The plan's definition of done is fixed. Weakening or skipping a test to pass is failure. An unimplemented piece is reported as incomplete in your summary, never a silent TODO.\n- The plan's code blocks were compiled and tested as one prototype, except where a phase says otherwise. A compile error is still a plan bug: fix the plan text in the same commit as the code.\n- Integer-only simulation state in `src/terraform/`; never `std/random` (use `terraform/keyrng`).\n- One writer per file set: work only in your own git worktree/branch. Land by rebasing on origin/main, fast-forwarding main and pushing (`git push origin HEAD:main`) after review passes; then delete your branch and remove any worktree you added.\n- Unit tests and debug builds are fine anywhere. Release builds, multi-seed batches, sweeps, the oracle and docker builds run on a pool worker (worker-2), never on hermes-hub, not even under `nice`.\n- Toolchain on hermes-hub: Nim 2.2.10 and nimby 0.2.3 in `~/.local/bin`; polyworld checkout at `~/code/polyworld`. A synced dependency directory is at `/home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/terraform-1a/deps`: `export TERRAFORM_DEPS=/home/ubuntu/.hermes/kanban/evidence/terraform-1a/deps` instead of syncing again. If `git -C $TERRAFORM_DEPS/polyworld rev-parse HEAD` is not the commit on line 1 of `terraform.lock`, sync your own `deps/` as the README says. On the MacBook: Nim 2.2.10, nimby 0.1.26 in `~/.local/bin`.\n- Secrets only via token broker: `token-broker exec --scope <scope> --reason \"...\" -- <cmd>`. OpenRouter scope is `openrouter` (`openrouter.inference` is deprecated). LLM calls in scripts/batches use the subscription pool first (`~/.hermes/plugins/pool-llm/bin/hermes-pool-llm`).\n- LLM spend cap for all of 1a: $250 (not yet confirmed by Dave). Stop and block before anything that would exceed it. No GPUs, no rented machines.\n- Never push to `example-org/polyworld` except its `terraform` branch.\n- Reviewer model: right before `kanban_request_review`, run `hermes kanban set-model $HERMES_KANBAN_WORKER_TASK claude-opus-5-5 --provider anthropic` (the review lane reuses a card's pinned model until the core fix lands). If the command is refused, put `reviewer-model: wanted claude-opus-5-5, set-model refused: <the error>` as the first line of your review summary.\n- Finish with `kanban_request_review` (review must be done by a different model than the author; neutral prompt: \"trace this and report what you observe\"). Summary reports what passes with test output, and what is incomplete.",
