+    "body": "Owner card for t_01a1ce32dab49fdd (state PR https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1235). The worker IAM role `hermes-worker` (account 123456789012, us-west-2) has no S3 access today. Until this terraform is applied, the new worker archive custody step refuses (`offbox_head_failed`) and deletes nothing, so scratch archives keep filling worker root disks.\n\n**Do (after PR1235 is merged into state):**\n1. In a state checkout at merged state: `cd hosts/hermes-workers/terraform && terraform init && terraform plan`.\n2. The plan must show ONLY these additions:\n   - `aws_s3_bucket` `hermes-worker-archives-123456789012`, plus its versioning, SSE, public-access-block and lifecycle resources (Glacier IR after 30 days; current versions never expire);\n   - `aws_iam_role_policy` `archives_write` on role `hermes-worker`.\n   \n   No replacement of instances or other resources. If the plan shows anything else, stop and comment the plan instead of applying.\n3. `terraform apply`.\n4. Verify from a worker (e.g. hermes-worker-1) with its instance role:\n   - `aws s3api head-object --bucket hermes-worker-archives-123456789012 --expected-bucket-owner 123456789012 --key scratch-archives/probe-missing` returns 404 (not 403);\n   - a `delete-object` attempt is AccessDenied.\n5. Live proof on one worker: `systemd-run --user --wait --collect -p RuntimeMaxSec=15min ~/.hermes/bin/hermes-core-python ~/bin/worker-disk-pressure --upload-budget-s 120`. Then check:\n   - the log line `archive_custody.uploaded` \u2265 1 if archives exist;\n   - receipts exist under `~/.hermes/archive/custody/<board>/`.\n\nRecord the plan summary, apply output and verification as a comment.\n\nConstraints: never grant `s3:DeleteObject*`; keep the explicit Deny statement.",
