+    "body": "Independent exact-head review of example-org/hermes PR #1492 (base `state`): https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1492\n\nReview exactly head `90e2a58e9d0a08f661c2ce9e072077b8c755be43` (branch `wt/land-lane-t01a1cfa4-r3`, three commits on state 05952b6128). You did not write this change; the build card is t_01a1cfa4fc605bbd. Do not push and do not merge.\n\n**What it is.** The serialized land lane, implementing the approved design `docs/designs/land-lane.md` rev 5 (carried in the PR; sha256 90719b556d435bfeb7f9ea72d1c691479f6c9229879ddec2887e9450695a5e26). The design is approved and not under review; review whether the code matches it. #1492 supersedes #1485 and #1462 (both closed): state kept moving onto `home/bin/hermes-core-wt-land` and headless force-push is refused, so each rebase got a new branch.\n\n**History.** Round 3 (t_01a1d0137bca9fe0, PR comment https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1485#issuecomment-6825903292) approved #1485 at 4e32cfbc7a with no blockers. Since then state gained ba49e0512f (\"core-wt ship: current repo name, identity reads once, no auth probe on worker gh\"), which conflicted in `main()`: state added `slug = canonical_slug(slug)` before `ev = dict(event=\"ship\", ...)` and the lane adds `lane=None` to that dict; the resolution keeps both. `git range-diff 05952b6128~0 ...` style check: `git range-diff 3e6c548ab1..4e32cfbc7a 05952b6128..90e2a58e9d` should show only that hunk changed. Confirm it, and check the lane against ba49e0512f's changes (canonical slug, identity cache, gh auth probe removal) \u2014 e.g. that the lane and `lane_probe`/`lane_evict_closed` use the canonical slug consistently. Then review the whole PR at the exact head. Round-3 advisories A (quota wait after the final lane CAS can outlast the skew fence) and B (no test of `--lane-enter` waiting out a brake) are deliberately left to a follow-up card, not this PR.\n\n**Get the code.** `token-broker exec --scope user/github --reason \"review PR 1492\" -- env GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=2 GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=credential.helper GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0= GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1=credential.helper GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1='!gh auth git-credential' git fetch https://github.com/example-org/hermes.git wt/land-lane-t01a1cfa4-r3` in a detached worktree of `~/.hermes/repos/hermes-state` (`git sparse-checkout disable`; remove the worktree when done). Confirm `git rev-parse HEAD` equals the sha above.\n\n**Check against** the spec's `## Implementation plan`, `## Invariants` and `## Acceptance` item 2:\n1. An approval only counts at its exact head; the lane never makes landable a head the gate would refuse.\n2. No lane-aware ship lands without the turn as checked in the CAS immediately before `land()`, and none rebases a pushed head without the turn.\n3. Every write is a compare-and-swap on the remote commit it read from; no write can erase a concurrent write.\n4. A writer removes only its own entry, non-live entries (skew margin for others), or blockers it saw merged/closed whose entry is unchanged; `lane release` is the logged exception.\n5. Lane unreachable, corrupt, version \u2260 1 or CAS exhausted refuses with exit 1 before any rebase or land; `disabled: true` and `HERMES_CORE_WT_LANE=off` bypass it.\n6. The exact-head review gate, the required checks and the review rule are unchanged for PRs outside the lane.\n\nRun `/usr/bin/python3 -m unittest tests.test_core_wt_land_lane tests.test_core_wt_ship_gate tests.test_core_wt_ci_proof tests.test_core_wt_quota tests.test_core_wt_land_spend tests.test_core_wt_deliver` (~8 min). Known environmental cases: `test_real_worker_cli_create_refusal_is_the_fence_ship_recognises` (installed CLI, gateway restarts) and `test_core_wt_ci_proof` during a live quota brake. State PRs have no CI checks.\n\nMake an adversarial pass; report only surviving findings, blocking separated from advisories.\n\n**Complete with** `kanban_complete` and `metadata` holding exactly these keys: `verdict` (\"approve\" or \"request_changes\"), `reviewed_sha` (the full 40-hex sha above, only if that is what you reviewed), `reviewed_pr` (exactly `https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1492`), and `findings`. Post the verdict as a PR comment naming the reviewed sha.",
