+    "body": "Follow-up to the land lane (build card t_01a1cfa4fc605bbd, PR https://github.com/example-org/hermes/pull/1492; design docs/designs/land-lane.md rev 5). Two non-blocking advisories from review t_01a1d0137bca9fe0 (PR #1485 @4e32cfbc7a), deliberately kept out of the lane PR so its reviewed delta stays a pure rebase:\n\nA. In `home/bin/hermes-core-wt-land` ship flow, after the final lane CAS (`lane.step(..., final=True)` just before `land()`), the PR-merge route's `gh.run('pr','merge')` runs `quota_preflight()`, which with the in-process quota wait (state b8180ba8b6) can sleep up to 3\u00d7(\u2264330 s + jitter) \u2248 16.7 min, longer than the 15-min SKEW fence. Fix: set `QUOTA_WAIT[\"enabled\"] = False` right after the final lane step passes (inside `if step.mode == \"on\":`, after the `expiring` check), so a brake there exits 75 and the rerun re-checks the turn. Add a test that fails without it.\n\nB. No test covers `--lane-enter` waiting out a short brake (the default path); the only brake test (`test_lane_ops_work_under_the_quota_brake_and_lane_enter_exits_75`) now runs with `HERMES_CORE_WT_QUOTA_WAIT=0`. Add one.\n\nStart only after PR #1492 (or its successor) is merged on `state` (check `git log origin/state -- home/bin/hermes-core-wt-land` contains the lane). Branch from current origin/state, open a state PR, get an independent exact-head review (fresh reviewer card pinned claude-opus-5-5/anthropic, metadata `verdict`, `reviewed_sha`, `reviewed_pr`), rebase-merge with `gh pr merge --rebase --match-head-commit`.",
