+    "title": "hermes-state: hub `label-probe <machine>` entry point for operator-call label_publish (core PR #1332)",
+    "body": "Follow-up from t_01a1cefefcad176a (core PR #1332, operator call `label_publish`). Core's hub executor runs `~/.local/share/hermes-worker-skills/bin/label-probe <machine>` (hermes_cli/kanban_operator_labels.py `_probe`, `PROBE_COMMAND`) as the hub-side proof. Until that probe exists, every label_publish fails closed with `proof_unavailable`.\n\n## Build (hermes-state, `state` branch, hosts/hermes-workers)\n- Add `bin/label-probe`. It is stdlib-only and takes one argument, a Board machine name (`[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}`). It runs as the hub user with the instance role. It resolves the machine to its running EC2 instance the same way `refresh-skill-labels` `targets()` does (active Board gateway plus the Name tag `hermes-<name>`). It then runs the same audited SSM read as `read_inventory()`.\n- Reuse the shared code, with no copy. Load `refresh-skill-labels` as a module, the way it already loads `publish-skill-labels`. Factor `read_inventory` so a probe run has **no side effects**: no `report_recovery`, no `deliver_incidents`, no cursor write.\n- Output contract: stdout is exactly one JSON object, `{\"machine\": <name>, \"complete\": true, \"skills\": [sorted skill:*], \"proofs\": {<capability:* label>: {\"ok\": bool, \"detail\": str}}}`. Filter `proofs` with `publish-skill-labels.valid_proofs` (CAPABILITIES only).\n- Exit non-zero, with a short stderr reason, when any of these hold: the machine is unknown or ambiguous, the inventory is incomplete or malformed, the read times out, or `proof_error` is set. Never print raw command output or secrets.\n- Add `label-probe` to `install-skill-refresh.py` `pairs`.\n- Tests go in `tests/test_refresh_worker_skills.py` or a sibling. Cover: the output shape, the no-side-effects guarantee, unknown machine, ambiguous instance, and incomplete inventory. Each test must fail without the fix.\n- Land per `references/state-pr-landing.md` (kanban-worker skill), then install it on the hub (`install-skill-refresh.py --files-only`). Verify that `label-probe worker-<n>` on the hub prints the contract.\n\n## Acceptance\n- With core #1332 live on the hub, a `label_publish` of an already-proven `capability:` label on a worker comes back `already_applied` or `applied`, not `proof_unavailable`. Show the operator_calls row (`hermes kanban supervisor-requests --operator-log`).",
