 - `setMachine` replaces the label set and appends a `machine_audit` row whose `change.labels` is sorted.\n   - `listGateways` returns `{gateways:[...]}`.\n   - `MAX_LABELS` is 32.\n   Cases to check: a racing write, a later dropped delta, and termination after `CAS_ROUNDS`.\n3. Job thread and lock behavior: `_claim`, `_run_job`, the stale-job bound, delivery retry and idempotency on replay. The dispatcher tick must never block on the probe or admin calls.\n4. Run the tests at head, in two batches:\n   - `scripts/run_tests.sh tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_operator_labels.py tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_operator_call.py`\n   - `scripts/run_tests.sh tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_supervisor_requests.py tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_foreign_card_writes.py tests/tools/test_kanban_tools.py`\n   \n   Also run `scripts/check`, and do at least one mutation of your own (for example, drop the `own != kol.HOME` guard in `apply_incoming`) to confirm the tests bite.\n5. Known gap: the hub `label-probe` executable is a hermes-state follow-up (t_01a1cf166d2629c3). Until it lands, calls fail closed with `proof_unavailable`. Judge whether that is acceptable for landing core first.\n\nComplete with `metadata.verdict` (`approve` or `request_changes`), `metadata.reviewed_sha` (40 hex) and `metadata.reviewed_pr` = 1332. Do not use `published_pr`. Do not merge.",
